  "scope_id": "BEYOND-CLASS2-20261027-001",
  "title": "Past class 2, hardness needs no three-way pair: a four-way Massey interaction is #P-hard where no pair can be",
  "subject": "The complexity of counting homomorphisms from 3-manifold groups into finite solvable groups",
  "conclusion": "For coprime p-group-by-cyclic targets on closed 3-manifolds with bounded first homology, hardness past class 2 does not need a three-way pair: a cross-layer hard pair already gives #P-hardness, and at r = 2, where no hard pair exists and class 2 is always polynomial, counting maps from 2-surgeries on knots into U4(F_p) x| <diag(1,-1,1,-1)> (p >= 5) is #P-hard, carried by a twisted triple Massey product read against a fourth class.",
